*.xsd.cs

# OpenCover UI analysis results
OpenCover/

# Azure Stream Analytics local run output
ASALocalRun/

# MSBuild Binary and Structured Log
*.binlog

# NVidia Nsight GPU debugger configuration file
*.nvuser

# MFractors (Xamarin productivity tool) working folder
.mfractor/

# Local History for Visual Studio
.localhistory/

# Visual Studio History (VSHistory) files
.vshistory/

# BeatPulse healthcheck temp database
healthchecksdb

# Backup folder for Package Reference Convert tool in Visual Studio 2017
MigrationBackup/

# Ionide (cross platform F# VS Code tools) working folder
.ionide/

# Fody - auto-generated XML schema
FodyWeavers.xsd

# VS Code files for those working on multiple tools
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.code-workspace

# Local History for Visual Studio Code
.history/

# Windows Installer files from build outputs
*.cab
*.msi
*.msix
*.msm
*.msp

# JetBrains Rider
*.sln.iml

# Result images
*.png

# Spike SIM-04 plausibility evidence figures (tracked deliverable, D-13)
!spike/figures/plausibility.png

# Phase-3 DATA-02 bulk training cache (large, regenerable, content-hash-named) — gitignored.
spike/data/cache/*
# …except the tiny committed round-trip / on-disk-schema fixture (D-04 smoke).
!spike/data/cache/fixture/

# graphify scratch output at repo root — machine-local (contains an absolute-path
# root marker) and fully regenerable. The GSD-canonical graph lives in .planning/graphs/.
graphify-out/

# Compiled manuscript output (Phase 10) — regenerable via manuscript/build.{ps1,sh}.
# Only the top-level build product is ignored; per-figure PDFs (e.g. the D-16 F1 figure)
# remain trackable deliverables.
manuscript/main.pdf

# Phase-9 Tapqir bridge (09-04): the CondaPkg materialized on-disk env — large and
# machine-local. The env SPEC (tapqir_env/Project.toml + Manifest.toml) stays tracked.
spike/comparator/tapqir_env/.CondaPkg/
# Phase-9 (09-01) inertness-check scratch: the pre-promotion Manifest snapshot used to
# prove the DataFrames/CSV promotion did not drift versions — not a deliverable.
spike/.manifest_baseline.toml

# Phase-5 (05-02) amortized-BF artifacts — large/regenerable caches, NOT deliverables.
# The trained ratio net + the Δρ-sweep hand-off draws + the KDE-baseline log-BF artifact
# are all reproducible from train_ratio.jl / bf.jl + spike/baseline/run_bf_baseline.jl.
spike/validation/trained_ratio.jld2
spike/validation/bf_sweep_draws.jld2
spike/baseline/bf_baseline_artifact.jld2

# Phase-5 (05-04) REPORTED-run artifacts — regenerable from run_sbc.jl / run_bf.jl /
# run_ood.jl at the LOCKED consts on VAL_MASTER_SEED. The committed deliverables are the
# run scripts; the .jld2 reports + PNG figures are reproducible outputs (numbers recorded
# verbatim in 05-04-SUMMARY.md).
spike/validation/sbc_report.jld2
spike/validation/bf_report.jld2
spike/validation/ood_report.jld2

# Phase-13 (13-11) training side effects: NeuralEstimators writes optimiser + train-state
# BSONs into the run's `savepath` alongside the loss history. The optimiser state is ~9 MB of
# machine state that is redundant with the persisted net, so it stays out of git…
spike/p13/three_way_train/*.bson
# …while the loss history itself is the evidence the run happened as reported, and stays
# tracked (it is why `savepath` is named explicitly rather than left in `tempdir()`).
!spike/p13/three_way_train/loss_per_epoch.csv
!spike/p13/three_way_train/train_time.csv

# Phase-8 external ground-truth corpus (D-04): downloaded image bytes stay OUT of git
# (large, licensed, regenerable from manifest + seeded fetch script + SHA-256 hashes).
corpus/data/*
# …except the tracked contract/test layer: the manifest, the tiny committed round-trip
# fixture, and the corpus .jl sources (which live outside corpus/data/ and stay tracked
# by default; the explicit negation keeps the fixture dir tracked even if empty).
!corpus/manifest.csv
!corpus/test/fixtures/
